{"authored" [{"question" "q-130478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $(CA)B=C(BA)$\n- $(A+A)B=2AB$\n- $CB=BC$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "5847a665e3d8835b0f7b5fc99a5435f269aed8ba5aac82bc9c4cc21d5f2bcba6" "basis" 1055 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I  is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $(CA)B=C(AB)$ is always true. However,  matrix multiplication is not commutative,   $AB\\ne BA$ in general. Therefore, $(CA)B\\ne C(BA)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+A)B=AB+AB=2AB$ is always true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, so $CB\\ne BC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "5847a665e3d8835b0f7b5fc99a5435f269aed8ba5aac82bc9c4cc21d5f2bcba6" "basis" 1055 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe" "basis" 1055 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/edb-import/verifica