ion" "q-75717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $CB=BC$\n- $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- $A(BC)=(AB)C$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069059/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea0efa5e94bd77a35d613848d33298e9018559b12d254e117581840a9e7087"} {"question" "q-75717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statement  III is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069059/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea0efa5e94bd77a35d613848d33298e9018559b12d254e117581840a9e7087"} {"question" "q-75717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069059/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "227ba6a893b014bcf74c8e6d4331bb840af0fc67168c576c6e8605e82c2f1033"} {"question" "q-75717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069059/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea0efa5e94bd77a35d613848d33298e9018559b12d254e117581840a9e7087"} {"question" "q-75717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] 